{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch58A954xG81yXh9dzyMa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`word_count` now counts words correctly when the text has extra spaces or newlines, and a new regression test covers it. All 4 tests pass.\n\n- **Cause** (`textkit/core.py`): the function used `text.split(\" \")`. That turns every run of extra spaces, and any space at the start or end, into empty \"words\". It also treated newlines and tabs as part of a word, so `\"a\\nb\"` counted as one.\n- **Fix:** it now uses `text.split()`, which splits on any run of whitespace and ignores whitespace at the start and end. Empty text and whitespace-only text now return 0.\n- **Test** (`tests/test_core.py`): `test_word_count_irregular_whitespace` checks repeated spaces, newlines (including blank lines), tabs, leading and trailing whitespace, an empty string and a whitespace-only string. I didn't run it against the old code, but `\"one  two   three\"` would have counted 6 there instead of 3."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":37662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0cb0271-9d2e-424b-9300-6520b087e648","uuid":"a5d81159-ee33-48ac-98ec-f1d4360bec75","timestamp":"2026-11-15T17:40:39.725Z","request_id":"req_011Ch58A8rRS511GiAY3VDJo"}
